    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Dual Constraint Temporary Waiver with Enhanced Safeguard Protocol: Issue a time-bounded dual waiver raising the FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.65 and the Noise ceiling to 85.0 dB for a defined production window (not to exceed 5 consecutive days). Mandatory compensating controls must be in place before execution: (a) mandatory PPE for all noise-exposed workers, (b) enforced 15-minute micro-break every 90 minutes, (c) daily health self-assessment check-ins, (d) on-call occupational health monitoring, and (e) automatic CBPA re-evaluation at the 72-hour mark. This option eliminates the deadline gap entirely but carries the highest worker health risk and must be reviewed and signed off by both the production manager and the safety officer. It should be treated as an emergency measure only.
