       Q: The formal priority_order lists only 'HumanWellbeing', yet the raw intent ordering places 'resource_efficiency' first — which governs when a 5–10% efficiency gain is achievable only by pushing operator fatigue from 0.2 up to (but not beyond) the 0.4 ceiling? Should wellbeing constraints be truly inviolable, or is a small fatigue trade-off acceptable for a significant efficiency improvement?
