    2. resource_efficiency (maximize, no upper bound or intensity cap)
       Q: There is no ceiling on how intensively the optimiser can operate to raise resource efficiency — should a maximum operating-intensity limit be set (e.g., throughput rate ≤ 120% of nominal, or total energy draw ≤ X kWh per shift) to prevent the optimiser from reaching a region where fatigue and noise constraints alone are insufficient guardrails and equipment stress accumulates undetected?
